{"connection_id": "BC-3a268fa911c6a83c90a6", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.3.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "Moses' face as fading glory", "note": "The commentary's bright face is set in a Moses-and-wrath complex; Paul rereads Moses' radiant face as the visible glory of the old covenant."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2dffff7231fbb00afe31", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.4.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's glory in Christ's face", "note": "The commentary links blessing with a radiant face; Paul locates the knowledge of God's glory in the face of Jesus Christ."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f3686d65732af65f3983", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.4.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "light of God's glory in Christ's face", "note": "The commentary makes divine favor visible on the face; Paul says God has shone in hearts to give the light of the knowledge of God's glory in the face of Christ."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8ddd960bd1fcd7fc97b9", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.5.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "each appears before the judgment seat", "note": "The commentary names the day of recompense; Paul says all must appear before Christ's judgment seat and receive according to what they did."}
{"connection_id": "BC-41065390f796ab6a61ed", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.5.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "aim to please the Lord", "note": "The commentary opens the scene with divine pleasure and closes it with judgment; Paul says his aim is to please the Lord before describing the judgment seat in the next verse."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fc3958c6351fd379deac", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.3.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "patience seeking repentance rather than perishing", "note": "The commentary contrasts a wrathful fall with repentance and a found way; Peter explains divine patience as not wishing people to perish but to come to repentance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-80a66cab0740806ce050", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.1.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "glory among the saints", "note": "The commentary names prophets, martyrs, and the righteous as companions; Paul says Christ comes to be glorified among his saints and marveled at by those who believed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d5410a43e094c1db01be", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.1.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "relief for the afflicted at revelation", "note": "The commentary sets wrath against the reward of the guided; Paul says the afflicted will receive relief when Jesus is revealed from heaven."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ec3ea0a38b158d144de5", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Thess.1.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "punishment at the Lord's revelation", "note": "The commentary names wrath coming upon a group; Paul describes punishment for those who do not know God and do not obey the gospel when the Lord is revealed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-484fa9ca4323c8d90c32", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.13.11", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "darkness falling on a judgment-blinded eye", "note": "The commentary gives anger a bodily eye-image and says something comes upon its recipient; Paul announces the Lord's hand against Elymas, after which mist and darkness immediately fall on him and he seeks a guide."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0b9cf8b6367c3796e1a3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.26.18", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "eyes opened, darkness turned to light, forgiveness", "note": "The commentary joins seeing, guidance, repentance, and favor; Paul's commission is to open eyes, turn people from darkness to light, and give forgiveness and an inheritance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-91c4565cc8e4513bc82e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.3.19", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "repentance, turning, and erased sins", "note": "The commentary makes repentance and a turn toward right guidance the way out of wrath; Peter calls hearers to repent and turn so that sins may be wiped out."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d247d108ff6649d31ae8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.4.33", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "great grace upon them all", "note": "The commentary's en'amte alayhim has an explicit giver and a group upon whom favor rests; Acts says great grace was upon all the witness-bearing community."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6a087224de0e84327c1e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.6.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Stephen's face like an angel's", "note": "The commentary treats the face as a bearer of a person's spiritual condition; Stephen's opponents see his face as that of an angel while he testifies before judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e586bc513ea7c901c5ea", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.7.41", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Stephen retells the calf", "note": "The commentary recalls the calf and Moses' anger; Stephen recounts Israel making the calf and offering sacrifice to the work of their hands."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3ad20f4f3e3e66c9b003", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.7.41", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "calf, sacrifice, and rejoicing", "note": "The commentary's calf episode is retold here with Israel making the calf, offering sacrifice to it, and rejoicing in what their hands made."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cfc1ee7300c9f41b5f90", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.7.42", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "God turns from persistent worship", "note": "The commentary links the calf with divine wrath; Stephen interprets Israel's idolatry as the point at which God turned away and gave them over to heavenly worship."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2ca98ef491d5a33e2a32", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.1.12", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "share the inheritance of the saints in light", "note": "The commentary names prophets and righteous among the favored; Paul gives thanks that believers are qualified to share the inheritance of the saints in light."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9214ae551e8f127216ce", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.1.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "transferred from darkness into the Son's kingdom", "note": "The commentary contrasts the guided with those who stray; Paul says God rescued people from darkness and transferred them into the kingdom of his beloved Son, where there is redemption and forgiveness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-41b90aa4bc13975dbca3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Col.1.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rescue from darkness into a kingdom", "note": "The commentary's divine deliverance moves people away from the lost side; Paul says the Father rescues people from the domain of darkness and transfers them to the Son's kingdom."}
{"connection_id": "BC-20061bb61c2b6f815f75", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.1.18", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "eyes of the heart enlightened for hope", "note": "The commentary makes the eye's condition carry guidance and favor; Paul prays for enlightened heart-eyes so believers know the hope of calling and inheritance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c6f7f11688f01cac47ab", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.3", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "children of wrath", "note": "The commentary's passive group is described as those upon whom wrath has fallen; Paul calls people by nature children of wrath, naming a condition before the following mercy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ece051620cacf4717388", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.3", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "children of wrath", "note": "The commentary ends with a collective named by wrath; Paul describes a former corporate condition as being children of wrath."}
{"connection_id": "BC-39d7bc530af224e2846d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.4", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God rich in mercy", "note": "The commentary contrasts those under wrath with those who receive favor; Paul turns immediately to God's great mercy and love for people."}

item.stdout:
{"connection_id": "BC-0439a491b8eea902162c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.4", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mercy interrupting a wrath condition", "note": "The commentary does not end at wrath but gives forgiveness a path onward; Paul immediately counters the prior wrath condition with God's rich mercy and great love."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a3a1a967284e3517be35", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.2.5", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "made alive by grace", "note": "The commentary sets wrath against the outcome of favor; Paul says people dead in trespasses are made alive with Christ by grace."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8f5425617eed542c5f36", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.5.14", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "Christ shining on one who rises", "note": "The commentary's eschatological face is lit after a fall or deathlike state; the cited hymn commands the sleeper to rise from the dead so Christ will shine upon that person."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3c66b2dc8f02a688f3cf", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.5.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "once darkness, now light; walk as light", "note": "The commentary joins the path to faces that shine or darken; Paul says the hearers were once darkness but are now light in the Lord and must walk as children of light."}
{"connection_id": "BC-99e5a75da487e5135192", "ref": "SBLGNT:Eph.5.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "formerly darkness, now light, therefore walk", "note": "The commentary's contrast joins identity, light, and a road; Paul says believers were darkness but are now light in the Lord and commands them to walk as children of light."}
{"connection_id": "BC-35c6891d6f61999d0b22", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.1.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "pleasing people or God", "note": "The commentary connects praise with approval and divine pleasure; Paul asks whether he seeks human approval or God's and says pleasing people would make him no servant of Christ."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d8fea315b00a4cccadf7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Gal.3.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "Christ becoming a curse for others", "note": "The commentary contrasts a group under anger with a group granted favor; Paul presents Christ as becoming a curse in order to redeem others from the law's curse, a different distributive account of adverse judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ba1bda48a66a70190822", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.11.39", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faithful witnesses await the promise", "note": "The commentary names prophets, truth-affirmers, martyrs, and the righteous as companions; Hebrews gathers faithful exemplars who were commended but had not yet received what was promised."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7a820262621399b57cc7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.11.40", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faithful made complete together", "note": "The commentary describes the favored as companions on one path; Hebrews says the earlier faithful are not made complete apart from the later community, extending the company across generations."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ceb0d5a37be8c7fc1290", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.11.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith pleases God", "note": "The commentary sets divine pleasure against wrath; Hebrews says faith is necessary to please God and that those who approach him must trust that he rewards those who seek him."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f1b5540ab28137f840cd", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.1", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "cloud of witnesses and shared race", "note": "The commentary calls the favored a group walking together; Hebrews pictures a cloud of witnesses surrounding the hearers as they run the race set before them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8733b21ebfe8efbf1a80", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.1", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "cloud of witnesses and a race to run", "note": "The commentary's favored way is a shared route with exemplary companions; Hebrews places believers within a cloud of witnesses and tells them to run the course set before them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-312bd4ded2059559b571", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.12.23", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "assembly of the righteous in heaven", "note": "The commentary lists prophets, truth-affirmers, martyrs, and righteous companions; Hebrews describes the assembly of the firstborn and the spirits of righteous people made complete."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d9db7fa4ce44371786aa", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "straying heart and unknown ways", "note": "The commentary ends with those who lose the path and those guided; Hebrews quotes God's complaint that the wilderness generation always goes astray in heart and has not known his ways."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f16ac5562afec74e4e85", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "anger and hearts always astray", "note": "The commentary binds divine anger to losing the right path; this wilderness interpretation says God was angry because the generation went astray in heart and did not know his ways."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8c655fc5924f38439a1e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's anger with the wilderness generation", "note": "The commentary says wrath comes upon a group after rebellion; Hebrews asks with whom God was angry for forty years and answers with those who sinned."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ce514e7805a4051f91b8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "angry forty years and fallen bodies", "note": "The commentary calls wrath a fall; Hebrews explicitly asks whether God was angry with those whose bodies fell in the wilderness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ad772443099a9e2e528a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.18", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "exclusion from rest", "note": "The commentary ties the day and the path to each group's end; Hebrews says the disobedient were barred by oath from entering God's rest."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a7efa8adb31741ff6c74", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.3.19", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "unbelief blocks entry", "note": "The commentary's lost group does not reach the guided path's end; Hebrews concludes that the wilderness generation could not enter because of unbelief."}
{"connection_id": "BC-499b660db56374a6effe", "ref": "SBLGNT:Heb.5.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "prayer with cries and tears", "note": "The commentary links the favored with prostration and weeping; Hebrews describes Jesus offering prayers and supplications with loud cries and tears, tying bodily humility to being heard."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6fefb575681e8afe7604", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.1.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "good gifts descend from above", "note": "The commentary describes benefaction as coming upon the favored; James says every good and perfect gift comes down from above from the Father of lights."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2a754eb137e9067c0107", "ref": "SBLGNT:Jas.1.20", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "human anger does not make justice", "note": "The commentary opposes wrath to favor and the straight way; James says human anger does not produce God's righteousness, an ethical warning about anger's outcome."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c5baf4a46cb5ddd18d31", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.11.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "walking at night and stumbling", "note": "The commentary's wrath-side loses the way and falls; Jesus's paired saying makes the night-walker stumble because light is not in that person."}
{"connection_id": "BC-06029598a1a48cec85af", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.11.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "walking in day without stumbling", "note": "The commentary joins correct guidance to light and an unfallen walk; Jesus says that a person walking in the day does not stumble because that person sees the world's light."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6005f244a3d53715d872", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.12.35", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "darkness overtakes a walker", "note": "The commentary says anger and error lose the road; Jesus says one walking in darkness does not know where one is going."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4b0af6cd829cc0f43140", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.12.43", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "human approval preferred to God's", "note": "The commentary asks whose judgment one approves and sets God's favor against anger; John says some loved human glory more than God's glory, explaining their refusal to confess Jesus."}
{"connection_id": "BC-266638680dd8d97b8d36", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.3.19", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "judgment as loving darkness rather than light", "note": "The commentary's two groups end in luminous or darkened conditions; Jesus explains judgment through the light's arrival and evildoers' love of darkness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cca595d7ee7290d4bc61", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.3.21", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "doing truth and coming to light", "note": "The commentary's favorable side joins right action to a found way; the one doing truth comes to the light so deeds can be seen as done in God."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e6188b75b1df67edb179", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.3.36", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrath remains upon the disobedient", "note": "The commentary's phrase describes people with wrath upon them; John says God's wrath remains on the one who disobeys the Son, alongside the alternative of eternal life."}
{"connection_id": "BC-41a6e894e7de6228c0f5", "ref": "SBLGNT:John.5.28", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the dead hear and come out", "note": "The commentary names the day of recompense for groups with different outcomes; Jesus speaks of the hour when all in the tombs hear his voice and come out."}

