{"connection_id": "BC-96904d95c5380e5b3714", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.5.12", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "rejoicing with the persecuted prophets", "note": "The commentary enumerates prophets and martyrs among the favored companions; Jesus tells the persecuted to rejoice because their reward is great and the prophets were persecuted before them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-27b01aea5d67087d77f5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.16", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "a face can be deliberately disfigured", "note": "The commentary reads faces as signs of inward outcomes; Jesus warns that hypocrites disfigure their faces to display fasting, showing that a visible religious face can be staged for human notice."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3267412d20edf850e596", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.16", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "disfigured faces seeking human notice", "note": "The commentary makes a face show an inward religious condition and begins with praise; Jesus criticizes fasters who disfigure their faces to be seen by people, distinguishing their received human reward from divine regard."}
{"connection_id": "BC-35a1bf7f997ece40e057", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wash your face in secret", "note": "The commentary gives the face a role in visible favor or wrath; Jesus tells the fasting person to wash and anoint the face so devotion is not performed for human observers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dce462236de7b71366ac", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anointed head and washed face before the Father", "note": "The commentary's favorable face is not merely a legal verdict; Jesus tells secret fasters to anoint the head and wash the face so the Father, rather than observers, sees and rewards."}
{"connection_id": "BC-963040a10c121bbc5cf7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.18", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the Father sees hidden devotion", "note": "The commentary says faces carry a visible mark of judgment; Jesus contrasts public appearance with the Father who sees what is hidden and rewards accordingly."}
{"connection_id": "BC-17c62bb4812d455e48c1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.22", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the healthy eye filling the body with light", "note": "The commentary's favorable eye is calm and bright; Jesus uses a healthy eye as the condition by which the whole body is full of light."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c93eb512207be8a1399d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.23", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bad eye and bodily darkness", "note": "The commentary's adverse face includes an afflicted eye and dark covering; Jesus's paired image makes the bad eye produce darkness throughout the body."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0bcbbd0814ac71008c6c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the broad road leads to destruction", "note": "The commentary ends with a guided path opposed to those who stray; Jesus contrasts the broad road that leads to destruction and the many who enter it."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f56d5c0c24d5f744b356", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wide way ending in destruction", "note": "The commentary's wrath side is a lost way and a fall; Jesus describes a broad way that leads to destruction and has many travelers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-56e3c990e82a66d5818f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.14", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the narrow path leads to life", "note": "The commentary asks to be guided to the straight path; Jesus says the narrow gate and hard way lead to life and are found by few."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9704cc71dbf6ee6a6ea8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.14", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "narrow way leading to life", "note": "The commentary's favored side is a found path; Jesus contrasts it with a narrow way that leads to life and is found by few."}
{"connection_id": "BC-edc937f5eb03b9578cd2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.8.11", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "company with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob", "note": "The commentary says the favored road is shared with exemplary companions; Jesus depicts many joining the patriarchs at the kingdom meal."}
{"connection_id": "BC-13aaff8a3fcc2604cac3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.8.12", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "outer darkness, weeping, and exclusion", "note": "The commentary gives the adverse group a dark, humiliated bodily condition; Jesus contrasts the kingdom meal with expulsion into outer darkness, weeping, and gnashing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3b9127683e2d1399e45b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Phil.2.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God works for his good pleasure", "note": "The commentary says the favored gift is actively bestowed; Paul says God works within the community both to will and to work for his good pleasure."}
{"connection_id": "BC-57179b493427760d9f25", "ref": "SBLGNT:Phil.2.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "shining lights among a crooked generation", "note": "The commentary contrasts the favored path with those who stray and says faces may shine; Paul calls believers blameless children of God who shine like lights in a crooked generation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5e6b49976f7284ad45f7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Phil.3.21", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lowly body transformed to glory", "note": "The commentary makes final grace visible in bodily appearance; Paul expects Christ to transform the lowly body into conformity with his glorious body."}
{"connection_id": "BC-93425a972ee27d3836d4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.14.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrath drunk by the idolater", "note": "The commentary's golden-calf warning culminates in divine anger; Revelation gives beast worshipers wine of God's wrath, a later apocalyptic pairing of idolatry and wrath."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e13d78a8af2318a94b83", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.14.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessed dead whose deeds follow them", "note": "The commentary names martyrs among those receiving favor; Revelation calls the dead who die in the Lord blessed, says they rest from toil, and says their deeds follow them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-660c9679cf072c2f475d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.14.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "idolatrous mark on forehead", "note": "The commentary turns the calf's idolatry into a wrath-bearing fate visible on the face; Revelation marks beast-worshipers on forehead or hand before announcing their judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9d597f418a341462f4fd", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.2.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hidden manna for the conqueror", "note": "The commentary recalls manna as an indicator of divine favor; Revelation promises hidden manna specifically to the one who conquers, relocating wilderness provision into an eschatological reward."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fba22ae3ad5af400d613", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.20.12", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "books opened for the dead", "note": "The commentary names the day of recompense; Revelation depicts the dead standing before the throne while books are opened and they are judged by their deeds."}
