{"connection_id": "BC-c93eb512207be8a1399d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.6.23", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bad eye and bodily darkness", "note": "The commentary's adverse face includes an afflicted eye and dark covering; Jesus's paired image makes the bad eye produce darkness throughout the body."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0bcbbd0814ac71008c6c", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the broad road leads to destruction", "note": "The commentary ends with a guided path opposed to those who stray; Jesus contrasts the broad road that leads to destruction and the many who enter it."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f56d5c0c24d5f744b356", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wide way ending in destruction", "note": "The commentary's wrath side is a lost way and a fall; Jesus describes a broad way that leads to destruction and has many travelers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-56e3c990e82a66d5818f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.14", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the narrow path leads to life", "note": "The commentary asks to be guided to the straight path; Jesus says the narrow gate and hard way lead to life and are found by few."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9704cc71dbf6ee6a6ea8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.7.14", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "narrow way leading to life", "note": "The commentary's favored side is a found path; Jesus contrasts it with a narrow way that leads to life and is found by few."}
{"connection_id": "BC-edc937f5eb03b9578cd2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.8.11", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "company with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob", "note": "The commentary says the favored road is shared with exemplary companions; Jesus depicts many joining the patriarchs at the kingdom meal."}
{"connection_id": "BC-13aaff8a3fcc2604cac3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Matt.8.12", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "outer darkness, weeping, and exclusion", "note": "The commentary gives the adverse group a dark, humiliated bodily condition; Jesus contrasts the kingdom meal with expulsion into outer darkness, weeping, and gnashing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3b9127683e2d1399e45b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Phil.2.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God works for his good pleasure", "note": "The commentary says the favored gift is actively bestowed; Paul says God works within the community both to will and to work for his good pleasure."}
{"connection_id": "BC-57179b493427760d9f25", "ref": "SBLGNT:Phil.2.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "shining lights among a crooked generation", "note": "The commentary contrasts the favored path with those who stray and says faces may shine; Paul calls believers blameless children of God who shine like lights in a crooked generation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5e6b49976f7284ad45f7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Phil.3.21", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lowly body transformed to glory", "note": "The commentary makes final grace visible in bodily appearance; Paul expects Christ to transform the lowly body into conformity with his glorious body."}
{"connection_id": "BC-93425a972ee27d3836d4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.14.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrath drunk by the idolater", "note": "The commentary's golden-calf warning culminates in divine anger; Revelation gives beast worshipers wine of God's wrath, a later apocalyptic pairing of idolatry and wrath."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e13d78a8af2318a94b83", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.14.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessed dead whose deeds follow them", "note": "The commentary names martyrs among those receiving favor; Revelation calls the dead who die in the Lord blessed, says they rest from toil, and says their deeds follow them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-660c9679cf072c2f475d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.14.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "idolatrous mark on forehead", "note": "The commentary turns the calf's idolatry into a wrath-bearing fate visible on the face; Revelation marks beast-worshipers on forehead or hand before announcing their judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9d597f418a341462f4fd", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.2.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hidden manna for the conqueror", "note": "The commentary recalls manna as an indicator of divine favor; Revelation promises hidden manna specifically to the one who conquers, relocating wilderness provision into an eschatological reward."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fba22ae3ad5af400d613", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.20.12", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "books opened for the dead", "note": "The commentary names the day of recompense; Revelation depicts the dead standing before the throne while books are opened and they are judged by their deeds."}
{"connection_id": "BC-24885cbc9c7584d0a475", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.20.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "book of life and the opposite end", "note": "The commentary divides groups by their final outcome; Revelation says those not found in the book of life are thrown into the lake of fire."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f54f29f4bf0d4f842ffd", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.20.4", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "martyrs share judgment and reign", "note": "The commentary includes martyrs among the favored companions; Revelation pictures those slain for their testimony seated on thrones, given judgment, and reigning with Christ."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a8699a73e5c4188d68a2", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.21.23", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's glory as the city's light", "note": "The commentary's blessed final side is luminous; Revelation says the eschatological city needs neither sun nor moon because God's glory gives it light."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2690e4115afba101a419", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.21.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "conqueror inherits and belongs to God", "note": "The commentary's favorable side receives a gift and shares a divine companionship; Revelation promises inheritance and a God-child relation to the one who conquers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-45ba0fadb9e12e141d77", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.21.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lake of fire for the unfaithful", "note": "The commentary's adverse group has an eschatological judgment distinct from the favored group; Revelation supplies the opposed fate for the cowardly, faithless, and idolaters."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b4457add510f2f72a87e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.22.3", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "no more curse", "note": "The commentary contrasts wrath with favor and the guided with the lost; Revelation's final city has no more curse, and God's servants worship there."}
{"connection_id": "BC-92679c67fa2947b36943", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.22.4", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "see God's face", "note": "The commentary says faces display the outcome of judgment; Revelation describes the servants seeing God's face and bearing his name on their foreheads."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dbb97fa7131b9043d5d8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.22.4", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "servants see God's face", "note": "The commentary's favorable final side has a transformed face; Revelation's servants see God's face and bear his name on their foreheads."}

item.stdout:
{"connection_id": "BC-676278af1f93ea7ed45b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.22.5", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's light on the final servants", "note": "The commentary's bright face belongs to a final favored community; Revelation says the Lord God will give light to his servants, with no more night."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f38c9f1e1e5633a643a8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.3.18", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "eye salve, white garments, and exposed shame", "note": "The commentary's two faces include afflicted eyes and visible favor; the risen Christ counsels the blind, naked church to obtain eye salve for sight and white garments to cover shame."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c40e4502e5c46eb0a0cd", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.4.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "elders fall and worship in praise", "note": "The commentary's chosen company prostrates in praise; the elders fall before the enthroned one, worship, and cast down their crowns."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e71214f59deb2ed7c1b6", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.6.16", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faces hidden from the enthroned one", "note": "The commentary reads the face as bearing the mark of wrath; Revelation's rulers and people ask to be hidden from the face of the enthroned one and from the Lamb's anger."}
{"connection_id": "BC-00ccfa21aa184ff0615a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.6.16", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hiding from the enthroned face and the Lamb's wrath", "note": "The commentary makes wrath and a face inseparable images; those facing judgment seek to hide from the face of the enthroned one and from the Lamb's wrath."}
{"connection_id": "BC-05fe8a722c527a488142", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.6.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the great day of wrath", "note": "The commentary calls the day the bearer of judgment; Revelation's terrified speakers ask who can stand when the great day of divine and Lamb's wrath has arrived."}
{"connection_id": "BC-381de7f24e98cf3a90b5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.6.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "great day of wrath", "note": "The commentary's yawm carries the two outcomes; Revelation calls the crisis the great day of their wrath and asks who can stand."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d22b6069e112b7125557", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.7.11", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "all heavenly attendants fall on their faces", "note": "The commentary joins the favored assembly to prostration; angels, elders, and living creatures fall before the throne on their faces and worship God."}
{"connection_id": "BC-81731b7f91ae2d0f48f3", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.7.16", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "no hunger, thirst, scorching, or heat", "note": "The commentary begins with wilderness food and ends with bodily marked destinies; Revelation's favorable multitude will neither hunger nor thirst and will not be struck by scorching heat."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1c143674a94b01184933", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.7.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the Lamb guides to living springs", "note": "The commentary says the favored are guided on a path and their faces show the outcome; Revelation's Lamb shepherds the multitude, guides them to springs of living water, and wipes away every tear."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c7f716739f19c0ed63c7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.7.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "guided to living water and tears wiped", "note": "The commentary couples a gifted community with guidance and a relaxed face; the Lamb shepherds the multitude to springs of living water and God wipes every tear from their eyes."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2eb773526184f4b98310", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rev.7.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "multitude before the throne", "note": "The commentary describes the favored as a community on one path; Revelation shows an uncountable multitude from every nation standing together before the throne and the Lamb."}
{"connection_id": "BC-aee1d9d293f72580def5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.1.18", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrath revealed from heaven", "note": "The commentary calls wrath something that descends upon people; Paul describes God's wrath as being revealed from heaven against ungodliness and unrighteousness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e413909769d297538cfd", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.11.22", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's kindness and severity", "note": "The commentary's rida-ghadaab contrast is expressed as two divine dispositions; Paul asks readers to consider God's kindness and severity, with continuance in kindness opposed to being cut off."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a60b852ccc0b7049815e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "glory, honor, and peace", "note": "The commentary sets two groups under judgment; Paul names glory, honor, and peace for everyone who does good, Jew first and Greek as well."}
{"connection_id": "BC-24f719e6d105d0308e1f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.10", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "glory, honor, and peace for doing good", "note": "The commentary's favorable side receives an approving divine outcome; Paul promises glory, honor, and peace to everyone who works good, against the wrath named in the same argument."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fc857f7152aee466865e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.29", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "praise from God, not people", "note": "The commentary describes hamd as approval; Paul says the true inward Jew receives praise from God rather than from human beings."}
{"connection_id": "BC-267d6ad71583719c298d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.5", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "day of wrath and judgment", "note": "The commentary names the day that bears wrath and recompense; Paul calls it a day of wrath and the revelation of God's righteous judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0d4a15c0dc632508526e", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.5", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "day of wrath and righteous judgment", "note": "The commentary calls yawm the days carrying punishment and forgiveness; Paul speaks of a day of wrath and revelation of God's righteous judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c0f3f69e43fd338fe1e1", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "glory, honor, and life for the patient", "note": "The commentary contrasts wrath with the outcome of the guided; Paul sets eternal life and glory for those who persevere in doing good against the day of judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fae6ea74ef1fe7c48713", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "eternal life for persevering good", "note": "The commentary's favor side includes faithful action and an ultimate outcome; Paul names eternal life for those persevering in good work and seeking glory, honor, and incorruptibility."}
{"connection_id": "BC-590dfcea9ce4f48864e4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrath for those who reject truth", "note": "The commentary distinguishes the wrath-struck from the guided; Paul describes wrath and fury for those who reject truth and follow unrighteousness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cdd742095e5a296184f7", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.2.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrath and anger for disobedience", "note": "The commentary makes wrath the adverse outcome of rebellion; Paul sets wrath and anger on those who reject truth and obey unrighteousness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-73fdb5739ef51d2e0cb4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.5.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "saved from wrath", "note": "The commentary contrasts those upon whom wrath falls with the forgiven; Paul says those justified by Christ's blood will be saved from wrath through him."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d0e25dfa0432f1e4189d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.5.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "justification and rescue from wrath through Christ", "note": "The commentary describes repentance, faith, good action, and guidance as the route beyond wrath; Paul frames rescue from wrath through Christ's blood, a distinct Christian account of the saving transition."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c4f61bb252c2cbb1977f", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.9.22", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "vessels of wrath and patience", "note": "The commentary contrasts a granted blessing with wrath falling on another group; Paul speaks of vessels of wrath and God's patience toward them, a close but not identical account of agency and judgment."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9e6e2256920ec59dab68", "ref": "SBLGNT:Rom.9.23", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "vessels of mercy prepared for glory", "note": "The commentary contrasts the wrath-struck with those granted favor; Paul pairs vessels of wrath with vessels of mercy prepared for glory, making the two-group contrast explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9d15301d9be67aec6e03", "ref": "1QS 3:13-4:26", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "two spirits and their paths", "note": "The commentary's two groups have opposed paths, visual states, and ends; the Community Rule's two-spirits instruction systematically assigns light and darkness, conduct, and judgment to opposed lots."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0af5c89feb087afcd5b9", "ref": "1QS 3:18-4:26", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "two spirits, paths, and outcomes", "note": "The commentary distinguishes two groups by the path they follow; the Community Rule describes opposing spirits that direct human conduct and lead to different outcomes at God's visitation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-548932710c67bbe87b17", "ref": "1QS 4:15-18", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "light, peace, and life of truth", "note": "The commentary's favored group walks a guided way and bears a softened face; the Community Rule associates the spirit of truth with enlightenment, peace, and life, giving a Jewish sectarian account of the favorable path."}

