{"connection_id": "BC-ea3899be50e8f5f6e9b7", "ref": "WLC:Ps.27.5", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew נעם as God's pleasantness", "note": "The source commentary says favor makes the face soft; the psalm seeks to behold the Lord's נעם in his house, using a Hebrew cognate for divine pleasantness or favor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ddb3b45840b0f48e3116", "ref": "WLC:Ps.30.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anger and favor in contrast", "note": "The commentary sets divine pleasure against wrath; this psalm contrasts a moment of divine anger with a lifetime of favor, giving that opposition a temporal shape."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c80f27c17707552ea506", "ref": "WLC:Ps.30.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anger set against favor", "note": "The commentary explicitly sets rida against ghadaab; the psalm compresses the same polarity into God's momentary anger and lifelong favor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f207ed01f8a8dc90bef0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.32.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "instruction with God's eye", "note": "The commentary joins the guided path to the eye's settled, favored state; the psalm promises instruction in the way to go and guidance with God's eye upon the learner."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a2243692748b29727185", "ref": "WLC:Ps.34.16", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's face against evildoers", "note": "The commentary says the face bears the outcome of favor or wrath; this psalm sets the Lord's face against evildoers, giving the contrary face-image an explicit judgment setting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8a9a3620c32ac14b8a66", "ref": "WLC:Ps.34.5", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "radiant faces without shame", "note": "The commentary contrasts faces marked by favor with faces marked by disgrace; here those who look to the Lord become radiant and are not ashamed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-123b257b86ef9f76b2cb", "ref": "WLC:Ps.34.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "looking to God, radiant faces, no shame", "note": "The commentary's favorable final face is luminous rather than humiliated; the psalm says those who look to YHWH are radiant and their faces are not ashamed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b3316e25ed5f102a8483", "ref": "WLC:Ps.37.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anger and wrath ruin the way", "note": "The commentary divides people by the path they take; Proverbs-like instruction in this psalm says to abandon anger and wrath because they lead toward evil."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3858b5b569d85c54a39c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.67.1", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessing and shining face", "note": "The commentary says bestowed favor is visible in the face; this prayer asks God to bless the people and make his face shine upon them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5844a6cfa6a8c1957658", "ref": "WLC:Ps.67.2", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's way made known", "note": "The commentary links bestowed favor with the path of those guided; this psalm asks that God's way and saving power become known among the nations after the face-shining blessing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-86f0065e52e904bc1fc6", "ref": "WLC:Ps.77.12", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "remembering God's deeds", "note": "The commentary explains God's days as remembered acts of punishment and pardon; this psalm says the worshipper will remember the Lord's works and meditate on them."}
