{"connection_id": "BC-871cf564dcde3cfaf5c2", "ref": "WLC:Neh.9.21", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "forty-year provision without lack", "note": "The commentary's ni'ma is an enduring divine favor rather than a single meal; Nehemiah says Israel lacked nothing for forty years, with garments and feet preserved in the wilderness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8fee3c3622c90108ebf3", "ref": "WLC:Neh.9.27", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "oppression, cry, and rescue", "note": "The commentary contrasts wrath with forgiveness; Nehemiah recounts Israel handed to enemies, crying to God, and receiving rescuers, a cycle of punishment and renewed favor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6f300fcecb52c5caa5a7", "ref": "WLC:Neh.9.28", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrath followed by rescue", "note": "The commentary says some receive punishment and others forgiveness; Nehemiah recounts that when Israel again did evil, God handed them over and later rescued them when they cried out."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6d5dd2a48916c0f3cea3", "ref": "WLC:Num.11.31", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "quail brought to camp", "note": "The commentary recalls quail among Israel's provision before warning of wrath; Numbers describes the wind bringing quail into the camp, supplying the wilderness scene behind that recollection."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d7274ae942e25a85ff44", "ref": "WLC:Num.11.31", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "quail brought by YHWH's wind", "note": "The commentary joins quail with a warning that wrath may descend; Numbers has YHWH bring quail to the camp immediately before its punitive outcome, preserving both food and danger in one scene."}
{"connection_id": "BC-eefbf6a383afbbf81e36", "ref": "WLC:Num.11.33", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "wrath during the meal", "note": "The commentary sets provision beside wrath coming upon people; here the Lord strikes while meat is still between their teeth, making that sequence explicit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2995d6d49a98460cccee", "ref": "WLC:Num.11.33", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "anger after the meat", "note": "The commentary's warning that transgression after provision brings wrath closely meets the account in which YHWH's anger flares against the people while the quail is still in their mouths."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7c4c341311abdd337827", "ref": "WLC:Num.11.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "manna before the people's eyes", "note": "The commentary gives ni'ma an eye-image while recalling manna; the dissatisfied wilderness people say that nothing is before their eyes except manna, an intentionally contrary eye-and-provision scene."}
{"connection_id": "BC-06b18fa55da77210ec09", "ref": "WLC:Num.14.18", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "Moses repeats the mercy formula", "note": "The commentary pairs divine wrath with the possibility of forgiveness; after Israel refuses to enter the land, Moses appeals to God's patience and forgiveness using the attributes revealed after the calf."}
{"connection_id": "BC-552a78f5c75dad6430d7", "ref": "WLC:Num.14.20", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "forgiveness after rebellion", "note": "The commentary contrasts the one upon whom wrath falls with those forgiven; after Moses' plea over Israel's rebellion, God answers that he has forgiven according to Moses' word."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ff50f5d0ffa8aa832050", "ref": "WLC:Num.6.25", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "shining face as blessing", "note": "The commentary says favor leaves a softened, cooled face; the priestly blessing asks God to make his face shine on the recipient, joining divine favor to a visible face."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a81e09ae6ba30b104de7", "ref": "WLC:Num.6.25", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "divine face shining with grace", "note": "The commentary's blessed side is visibly softened and bright; the priestly blessing asks that YHWH's face shine upon the people and be gracious to them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f276ba7d9283adbc0421", "ref": "WLC:Num.6.26", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lifted face and peace", "note": "The commentary reads the favored group as bearing a softened face; the blessing asks God to lift his countenance upon Israel and give peace, making face and favorable outcome a single formula."}
{"connection_id": "BC-debd4951c8b16e823923", "ref": "WLC:Num.6.26", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lifted face and peace", "note": "The commentary contrasts a burdened face with a favored one; the blessing asks YHWH to lift his face toward the people and give them peace."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4a5e2d15349bf4a1b1ae", "ref": "WLC:Prov.12.2", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "good person obtains favor, schemer condemned", "note": "The commentary relates approval and praise to the contrary of wrath; Proverbs says a good person obtains favor from YHWH while a person of schemes is condemned."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3c5033f17c2d6089619d", "ref": "WLC:Prov.13.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "good understanding gives favor, treacherous way is hard", "note": "The commentary sets favor against the condition of the lost way; Proverbs joins good understanding that gives favor to the hard way of the treacherous."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8ae34f663d67f2b6b3ea", "ref": "WLC:Prov.14.35", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "royal favor versus wrath toward shame", "note": "The commentary opposes favor and wrath and reads abasement in the adverse side; Proverbs gives the same pair in a king's favor for a prudent servant and wrath toward a shameful one."}
{"connection_id": "BC-9baf216103e5fc8b4e9b", "ref": "WLC:Prov.15.1", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "softness turns wrath aside", "note": "The commentary opposes a softened face to anger's scowl; Proverbs says a soft answer turns wrath away while a harsh word stirs it up."}
{"connection_id": "BC-64fa35945255be318d7f", "ref": "WLC:Prov.15.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "joy alters the face", "note": "The commentary says favor makes the face soft while anger makes it sullen; Proverbs says a glad heart makes the face cheerful, while sorrow breaks the spirit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4d6f57d615f2749e51c4", "ref": "WLC:Prov.15.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "joyful heart making a face good", "note": "The commentary reads inner favor or anger through the face; Proverbs similarly says a joyful heart makes the face good while sorrow crushes the spirit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7575ba244f4794f43685", "ref": "WLC:Prov.15.30", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "light of eyes refreshes the heart", "note": "The commentary says favor cools and settles the eye; Proverbs says light to the eyes gladdens the heart and good news refreshes the bones, a specific bodily image of restored well-being."}
{"connection_id": "BC-05b7555b2d458db61643", "ref": "WLC:Prov.15.30", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "light of the eyes gladdening the heart", "note": "The commentary's ni'ma image is an eye made calm and refreshed; Proverbs links the light of the eyes with a glad heart and bodily renewal."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6dd55585ae28967eccd0", "ref": "WLC:Prov.16.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "bright royal face and rain", "note": "The commentary contrasts the face marked by wrath with the softened face of favor; Proverbs says a king's bright face means life and his favor is like a spring rain cloud."}
{"connection_id": "BC-fe246d25991d2b8ea946", "ref": "WLC:Prov.16.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "light of a king's face and rainlike favor", "note": "The commentary's favorable face is soft and bright, and its blessing descends; Proverbs says life is in the light of a king's face and his favor is like a latter-rain cloud."}
{"connection_id": "BC-60abf56d15a111faed9b", "ref": "WLC:Prov.16.24", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew נעם words heal", "note": "The source commentary gives softness and gentleness as a branch of ن ع م; Proverbs calls words of נעם sweet as honey and healing to the bones, a cognate used for soothing speech and bodily benefit."}
{"connection_id": "BC-31e9fa9b96cd5a708f6e", "ref": "WLC:Prov.19.12", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrath and favor as bodily weather", "note": "The commentary's contrast is between anger's harsh face and bestowed good; Proverbs compares a king's anger to a lion's growl and his favor to dew on grass."}
{"connection_id": "BC-869d50309676bab89d25", "ref": "WLC:Prov.19.12", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "wrath like lion and favor like dew", "note": "The commentary contrasts an overwhelming anger with a gentle blessing that comes upon people; Proverbs compares a king's wrath to a lion's roar and his favor to dew on grass."}
{"connection_id": "BC-42cff8f3c92a3b770c20", "ref": "WLC:Prov.28.13", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "confessing and forsaking sins obtains mercy", "note": "The commentary's route out of wrath includes repentance and changed conduct; Proverbs contrasts hiding transgressions with confessing and forsaking them in order to receive mercy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-96263474811ea6f32888", "ref": "WLC:Prov.3.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew נעם and peaceful paths", "note": "The commentary links the ن ع م family with good and praise; Proverbs uses Hebrew נעם for wisdom's pleasant ways and says all her paths are peace, joining the cognate to a favored way."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1d91866a10902f0ad8f8", "ref": "WLC:Prov.3.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "no'am joined to ways of peace", "note": "The commentary associates the n-' -m family with a softened favorable condition and a path; Proverbs calls wisdom's ways ways of no'am, pleasantness, and all her paths peace."}

