{"connection_id": "BC-4f34bf6a59a90ebc7c95", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "paths of steadfast love", "note": "The commentary describes a way belonging to those receiving favor; the psalm asks God to remember his mercy and steadfast love, which have marked his dealings from of old."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b859c59a0465f1804ff0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.25.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "humble people taught the way", "note": "The commentary asks for guidance onto the straight path; this psalm says God guides the humble in justice and teaches them his way."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ea3899be50e8f5f6e9b7", "ref": "WLC:Ps.27.5", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew נעם as God's pleasantness", "note": "The source commentary says favor makes the face soft; the psalm seeks to behold the Lord's נעם in his house, using a Hebrew cognate for divine pleasantness or favor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ddb3b45840b0f48e3116", "ref": "WLC:Ps.30.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anger and favor in contrast", "note": "The commentary sets divine pleasure against wrath; this psalm contrasts a moment of divine anger with a lifetime of favor, giving that opposition a temporal shape."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c80f27c17707552ea506", "ref": "WLC:Ps.30.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anger set against favor", "note": "The commentary explicitly sets rida against ghadaab; the psalm compresses the same polarity into God's momentary anger and lifelong favor."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f207ed01f8a8dc90bef0", "ref": "WLC:Ps.32.9", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "instruction with God's eye", "note": "The commentary joins the guided path to the eye's settled, favored state; the psalm promises instruction in the way to go and guidance with God's eye upon the learner."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a2243692748b29727185", "ref": "WLC:Ps.34.16", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's face against evildoers", "note": "The commentary says the face bears the outcome of favor or wrath; this psalm sets the Lord's face against evildoers, giving the contrary face-image an explicit judgment setting."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8a9a3620c32ac14b8a66", "ref": "WLC:Ps.34.5", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "radiant faces without shame", "note": "The commentary contrasts faces marked by favor with faces marked by disgrace; here those who look to the Lord become radiant and are not ashamed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-123b257b86ef9f76b2cb", "ref": "WLC:Ps.34.6", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "looking to God, radiant faces, no shame", "note": "The commentary's favorable final face is luminous rather than humiliated; the psalm says those who look to YHWH are radiant and their faces are not ashamed."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b3316e25ed5f102a8483", "ref": "WLC:Ps.37.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anger and wrath ruin the way", "note": "The commentary divides people by the path they take; Proverbs-like instruction in this psalm says to abandon anger and wrath because they lead toward evil."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3858b5b569d85c54a39c", "ref": "WLC:Ps.67.1", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessing and shining face", "note": "The commentary says bestowed favor is visible in the face; this prayer asks God to bless the people and make his face shine upon them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-5844a6cfa6a8c1957658", "ref": "WLC:Ps.67.2", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's way made known", "note": "The commentary links bestowed favor with the path of those guided; this psalm asks that God's way and saving power become known among the nations after the face-shining blessing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-86f0065e52e904bc1fc6", "ref": "WLC:Ps.77.12", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "remembering God's deeds", "note": "The commentary explains God's days as remembered acts of punishment and pardon; this psalm says the worshipper will remember the Lord's works and meditate on them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-52f9beb2b81a4e999448", "ref": "WLC:Ps.77.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God's wonders among peoples", "note": "The commentary calls for recalling God's acts across history; the psalm says God works wonders and makes his strength known among the peoples."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d00138f9bb98ba3c1530", "ref": "WLC:Ps.77.21", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God leads like a shepherd", "note": "The commentary describes those guided together on a path; the psalm concludes its exodus recollection with God leading his people like a flock through Moses and Aaron."}
{"connection_id": "BC-130daba4bcff96a66f1f", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.29", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "quail and satisfaction", "note": "The commentary names manna and quail as gifts preceding the warning; this retelling says Israel ate and was filled after God brought the birds."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d0238b1ffd8fac75c4a1", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.31", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "wrath after appetite", "note": "The commentary sets the bestowed food against wrath; this wilderness retelling says God's anger rose against the well-fed people and struck them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a13ed2d1c147a865a7a1", "ref": "WLC:Ps.78.39", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "mercy turns wrath aside", "note": "The commentary places wilderness wrath beside forgiveness; this retelling says God remembered Israel's mortality and repeatedly turned away his anger instead of destroying them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2b2a5d483062615cfa77", "ref": "WLC:Ps.80.4", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "face shining brings salvation", "note": "The commentary connects divine favor, a shining face, and deliverance; the refrain asks God to restore the people, make his face shine, and save them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ef7422ad9d19c42f28e2", "ref": "WLC:Ps.80.5", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anger against the people's prayer", "note": "The commentary contrasts divine anger with favor; the community asks how long God will be angry at its prayer, making worship itself the setting of the wrath question."}
{"connection_id": "BC-50c7b8c9ff829da81cd3", "ref": "WLC:Ps.80.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "restoration through a shining face", "note": "The commentary links the two outcomes to faces and says favor softens the face; the community asks God to restore them, make his face shine, and save them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8cb2f1d7e9f25d3db4b5", "ref": "WLC:Ps.85.4", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anger removed for restoration", "note": "The commentary contrasts wrath with favor; this community prayer says God has taken away anger and turned from fierce wrath after restoring the land."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2ac887072763d42e7b9e", "ref": "WLC:Ps.85.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mercy and salvation shown", "note": "The commentary says others receive forgiveness instead of wrath; the psalm asks God to show steadfast love and grant salvation to the people."}
{"connection_id": "BC-de3d7342c9dcb19437b7", "ref": "WLC:Ps.89.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessed people walk in face-light", "note": "The commentary joins the favored group to a shared path and visible faces; the psalm calls blessed the people who walk in the light of God's countenance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0f9c028d8445d6f4e86a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.90.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew נֹעַם upon the people", "note": "The commentary's ن ع م family includes favor and softness; the psalm asks that the Lord's נֹעַם be upon the people and their work, a Hebrew cognate used for divine favor or pleasantness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-204e768a06b4c635e839", "ref": "WLC:Ps.90.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "no'am of God upon us", "note": "The commentary's n-' -m family joins bestowed favor to softness; Hebrew no'am, a cognate form, asks that God's pleasantness or favor be upon us, closely matching the favor-upon-a-group construction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e3b59cf722590cacb064", "ref": "WLC:Ps.99.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "forgiveness with accountability", "note": "The commentary sets pardon beside wrath; the psalm says God answered Israel and forgave them while also dealing with their deeds, holding mercy and judgment together."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4a044e7f7b6264ea9e4f", "ref": "WLC:Zech.3.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "walking God's ways among those standing before him", "note": "The commentary calls the righteous a company on the favored road; the high priest is promised access among those standing before God if he walks in God's ways."}
{"connection_id": "BC-53663bfa35b0774bf179", "ref": "WLC:Zeph.1.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "day of wrath and distress", "note": "The commentary identifies the day as carrying wrath; Zephaniah calls the Lord's day a day of wrath, distress, ruin, darkness, and gloom."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e0bc3f008ddf4c8d00e8", "ref": "WLC:Zeph.1.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew יום in the day of wrath", "note": "The source commentary labels Arabic يَوْم and root ي و م, then explains ayyam Allah as days of punishment and pardon; Zephaniah uses the Hebrew cognate יום for the Lord's day of wrath and distress."}

