{"connection_id": "BC-2b2a5d483062615cfa77", "ref": "WLC:Ps.80.4", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "face shining brings salvation", "note": "The commentary connects divine favor, a shining face, and deliverance; the refrain asks God to restore the people, make his face shine, and save them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ef7422ad9d19c42f28e2", "ref": "WLC:Ps.80.5", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anger against the people's prayer", "note": "The commentary contrasts divine anger with favor; the community asks how long God will be angry at its prayer, making worship itself the setting of the wrath question."}
{"connection_id": "BC-50c7b8c9ff829da81cd3", "ref": "WLC:Ps.80.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "restoration through a shining face", "note": "The commentary links the two outcomes to faces and says favor softens the face; the community asks God to restore them, make his face shine, and save them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8cb2f1d7e9f25d3db4b5", "ref": "WLC:Ps.85.4", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "anger removed for restoration", "note": "The commentary contrasts wrath with favor; this community prayer says God has taken away anger and turned from fierce wrath after restoring the land."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2ac887072763d42e7b9e", "ref": "WLC:Ps.85.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "mercy and salvation shown", "note": "The commentary says others receive forgiveness instead of wrath; the psalm asks God to show steadfast love and grant salvation to the people."}
{"connection_id": "BC-de3d7342c9dcb19437b7", "ref": "WLC:Ps.89.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessed people walk in face-light", "note": "The commentary joins the favored group to a shared path and visible faces; the psalm calls blessed the people who walk in the light of God's countenance."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0f9c028d8445d6f4e86a", "ref": "WLC:Ps.90.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew נֹעַם upon the people", "note": "The commentary's ن ع م family includes favor and softness; the psalm asks that the Lord's נֹעַם be upon the people and their work, a Hebrew cognate used for divine favor or pleasantness."}
{"connection_id": "BC-204e768a06b4c635e839", "ref": "WLC:Ps.90.17", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "no'am of God upon us", "note": "The commentary's n-' -m family joins bestowed favor to softness; Hebrew no'am, a cognate form, asks that God's pleasantness or favor be upon us, closely matching the favor-upon-a-group construction."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e3b59cf722590cacb064", "ref": "WLC:Ps.99.8", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "forgiveness with accountability", "note": "The commentary sets pardon beside wrath; the psalm says God answered Israel and forgave them while also dealing with their deeds, holding mercy and judgment together."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4a044e7f7b6264ea9e4f", "ref": "WLC:Zech.3.7", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "walking God's ways among those standing before him", "note": "The commentary calls the righteous a company on the favored road; the high priest is promised access among those standing before God if he walks in God's ways."}
{"connection_id": "BC-53663bfa35b0774bf179", "ref": "WLC:Zeph.1.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "day of wrath and distress", "note": "The commentary identifies the day as carrying wrath; Zephaniah calls the Lord's day a day of wrath, distress, ruin, darkness, and gloom."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e0bc3f008ddf4c8d00e8", "ref": "WLC:Zeph.1.15", "target": "sec6", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "soydas", "basis": "Hebrew יום in the day of wrath", "note": "The source commentary labels Arabic يَوْم and root ي و م, then explains ayyam Allah as days of punishment and pardon; Zephaniah uses the Hebrew cognate יום for the Lord's day of wrath and distress."}

